user
limit.js exports pLimit(n), which should run at most n async tasks at a time and return, for each call, a promise of that task's result. It has bugs: it can exceed the limit, and a task that rejects can stall the rest of the queue. Fix it so the limit always holds, every task's own promise resolves or rejects with that task's outcome, and a failure never blocks later tasks. Verify with: node test.js
